"Open Platform\nDocumentation\nSupport Center\nAnnouncement\nConsole\nAI Assistant \nEnglish\nLog In\n\nTables of Contents\n\nGetting Started\n > \nDeveloper account registration\n1. Signing up\n2. Understanding Shopee Open Platform account types\n3. Shopee Open Platform Eligibility Criteria\n3.1 Shopee Sellers\n3.2 Third-party Partner Platforms\n4.Submitting profile details for approval\n4.1 Log in to Shopee Open Platform > Console > App Management > App List > choose an account type depending on which description suits your business profile better.\n4.2 Fill in the details according to your account type\n4.2.1 Shopee Seller > Individual Seller\n4.2.2 Shopee Seller > Registered Business Seller\n4.2.3 Third-party Partner Platform\n4.3 Wait for your profile to be approved by Shopee\nGetting Started\nIntroduction\nDeveloper account registration\nApp management\nService Market\nAPI calls\nPush Mechanism notifications\nAuthorization and Authentication\nSandbox Testing V2\nService Partner Program\nV2.0 API Call Flow\nCNSC API Integration Guide\nKRSC API Integration Guide\nV2.0 Data Definition\nRequesting Access to Sensitive Data\nTW New Developer Audit\nBR SPI App Creation User Guide\nBRASIL | Jornada do Desenvolvedor\nSua trilha começa aqui!\nDesenvolva uma integração\nCrie um login\nCrie a conta de desenvolvedor\nCrie seu App\nRealize testes (Sandbox)\nPublique seu App (Go Live)\nAutorize sua primeira loja\nDados Sensíveis (Sensitive Data)\nFaça sua primeira chamada de API\nPush Notifications (Webhooks)\nPerguntas Frequentes\nReferências\nBoas práticas antes de abrir um ticket\nAPI Guidelines and Flows\nGuidelines for Creating Product\nProduct creation preparation\nCreating product\nCreating global product\nPublishing global product\nVariant management\nProduct base info management\nStock & Price Management\nOrder Management\nFirst Mile Binding\nReturn Refund Management\nSIP best practices\nShopee On-Platform Ads API Guide\nShopee Xpress - Package-free Integration Guide\nBRAZIL | Specific Local Guides\nAPIs de Order (Pedido)\nAPIs de Logistics (Logística)\nComo subir a NF-e através da OpenAPI e Mascaramento de Dados\nAUTO PARTS: COMPATIBILIDADE DE AUTOPEÇAS\nShopee Entrega Direta\nFulfilled by Shopee (BR)\nLogística do Vendedor (API de Cotação)\nTurbo Delivery (Quotation API)\nFerramenta de Log da Open Platform\nInstant Mart Integration Guide\nLivestream API Integration Guide\nShopee AMS API Integration Guide\nShopee Video API Integration Guide\nBrand Portal Service API Integration Guide\nInstant Order Fulfillment Guide\nTerms of Use\nTerms of Service\nData Protection Policy\nPlatform Partner Rules\nTW Developer Screening\nChatbot Terms of Service\nDeclare seus IPs\nDeveloper account registration\nLast Updated: 2026-09-10\nLanguage Supported: English / 简体中文 / 繁體中文 / Português (Brasil) / ไทย\n\nThere are 2 key stages to creating a Shopee Open Platform account:\n\n(A) Signing up\n\n(B) Submitting profile details for approval\n\nRead more about the steps below.\n\n\n\n\n1. Signing up\n\n\n\n\n1.1 From the Shopee Open Platform homepage, select Log In > select Sign up > fill in your email address\n\n\n\n\n⚠️ Note: Account’s email cannot be changed once registered.\n\n\n\n\n1.2 Check the inbox of your submitted email address for a verification code email from us.\n\n⚠️Note: If you don’t see the email, check your Junk folder first. If there is still no email from us, select Resend.\n\n1.3 Input the verification code that you got from the email and set your password.\n\n\n\n\n1.4 Once the password is set successfully, the page will automatically log in to your account, and you can view the open platform page.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n⚠️Note: Before you can submit your profile details for approval (Section 4.), you need to understand which account type best suits your business, and the eligibility criteria for each.\n\n2. Understanding Shopee Open Platform account types\n\n\n\n\nIndividual Seller - Accounts of individuals who sell on Shopee without a business license.(Only support service your Shopee shop. Closed for BR)\nRegistered Business Seller - Accounts of businesses selling on Shopee with a registered license.(Only support service your Shopee shop.)\nThird-party Partner Platform (ISV) - Accounts of businesses with registered licenses providing services to sellers on Shopee.\n\n\n\n\nYou can use the Account Type Selection table below to see which account type you should choose. Note that:\n\nThe APPs you can create on Shopee Open Platform depends on the account type you apply for. Refer to App management page for details.\nAdditionally, you need to meet the Shopee Open Platform Eligibility Criteria based on the markets you’re operating in and the account type you want to apply for.\nAccount Type Selection\nAre you a Shopee seller?\tAre you an individual or an enterprise?\tWhich Account Type should you choose?\tDescription\nYes\tIndividual\tShopee Seller > Individual Seller\tAccounts of individuals who sell on Shopee without a business license.(Note: You can only provide software services to your own Shopee shop.)\nYes\tEnterprise\tShopee Seller > Registered Business Seller\tAccounts of enterprises selling on Shopee with a registered license.(Note: You can only provide software services to your own Shopee shop.)\nNo\tThird-party Partner Platform (ISV)\tAccounts of enterprises with registered licenses providing services to sellers on Shopee.\n3. Shopee Open Platform Eligibility Criteria\n\n\n\n\nView the eligibility criteria below for different account types:\n\nShopee Seller\nThird-party Partner Platform\n\n\n\n\n[For cross-border Third-party Partner Platforms]\n\nNotify your Account Manager before you apply. If your company is registered in China, refer to Shopee企业ERP应用管理方案 for more information.\n\n3.1 Shopee Sellers\n\n\n\n\nTo gain access to Shopee Open Platform, you have to meet the criteria of the market(s) you’re operating in:\n\nMarket\tSeller Criteria\nSG (Singapore)\t1. Individual Seller to provide valid personal identification documents during your application.\n2. Registered Business Seller to provide valid business documents during your application.\tMall Sellers ORManaged Sellers ORSellers with at least 30 orders in the last 30 days\nMY (Malaysia)\tMall Sellers OR\nRegistered Business Sellers OR\nSellers with minimum 1 order in L12M\nTH (Thailand)\tMall Sellers ORManaged Sellers\nTW (Taiwan)\tMall Sellers.\nID (Indonesia)\tMall Sellers ORManaged Sellers ORSellers with at least 30 orders in the last 30 days.\nVN (Vietnam)\tPreferred Sellers OR Mall Sellers.\nPH (Philippines)\tMall Sellers ORManaged Sellers ORSellers with at least 600 orders in the last 30 days.\nMX (Mexico)\tN/A\nCO (Colombia)\tN/A\nCL (Chile)\tN/A\nCB-KR (Cross Border-Korea)\tN/A\nCB-JP (Cross Border-Japan)\tN/A\nBR (Brazil)\tRegistered business sellers with valid business documents in Brazil, and at least 1 order in the last 30 days.\nCB-CN (Cross Border- China)\tRegistered business sellers with valid business documents in China with at least 30 orders in the last 30 days.(Notify your Account Manager before you apply.)\n3.2 Third-party Partner Platforms\n\n\n\n\nTo gain access to the Shopee Open API Platform, you have to meet the following criteria:\n\n\n\n\nYou’re a registered business. Provide valid business documents during your application.\nYour business product has to be live, with existing ecommerce integrations which are identifiable via a provided trial account.\nYour services should not include suspicious activities such as the selling of cross-border accounts, or extracting listing information to enable transactions outside of Shopee. You may refer to our Platform Partner Rules for more information.\nSubmit live versions of (a) your business product’s URL, (b) trial account login details and enable all features for Shopee’s testing purposes.\nYour live business product URL must use HTTPS (https://), support TLS 1.2 or higher, and maintain a security rating of “A”\n\n\n\n\nIf you are a developer registered in the regions stated below, take note of the additional criteria that applies to you:\n\nTW (Taiwan)\n\nYour existing ecommerce integration(s) must be with a major ecommerce platform that has regulations for user data privacy.\n\n\n\n\nCB-CN (Cross Border-China)\n\nThe business scope of your business license must be software development.\nYour registered capital must be higher than 100,000 RMB.\nYou should have notified your Account Manager regarding your application.\n\n\n\n\nCB-KR (Cross Border-Korea), CB-JP (Cross Border-Japan)\n\nYou should have notified your Account Manager regarding your application.\n4.Submitting profile details for approval\n4.1 Log in to Shopee Open Platform > Console > App Management > App List > choose an account type depending on which description suits your business profile better.\n\n\n\n\n⚠️Note: See the Understanding Shopee Open Platform account types section below for more details on eligibility.\n\n*Shopee Open Platform Console: Refers to the site for you to manage all Shopee Open Platform matters.\n\n4.2 Fill in the details according to your account type\n\n\n\n\nA. Shopee Seller > Individual Seller\n\nB. Shopee Seller > Registered Business Seller\n\nC. Third-party Partner Platform\n\n4.2.1 Shopee Seller > Individual Seller\n\n\n\n\ni) After selecting Shopee Seller as your account type, you will be redirected to verify your Shopee seller account. Fill in the correct Shopee seller account credentials > select Log In to complete verification.\n\nii) If your seller account verification is successful, you can continue to fill in other Shopee Seller Identification details.\n\nSelect Individual Seller from the Seller Type dropdown menu > fill in your Key Account Manager’s Email > select Next.\n\n⚠️Note: Key Account Manager's Email should be a valid Shopee email (ends with @shopee.com). If no Key Account Manager's Email, please leave it blank.\n\n\n\n\niii) Fill in all profile details > select Submit.\n\n\n\n\n4.2.2 Shopee Seller > Registered Business Seller\n\n\n\n\ni) After selecting Shopee Seller as your account type, you will be redirected to verify your Shopee seller account Fill in the correct Shopee seller account credentials > select Log in to complete verification.\n\nii) If your seller account verification is successful, you can continue to fill in other Shopee Seller Identification details.\n\nSelect Registered Business Seller from the Seller Type dropdown menu > fill in your Key Account Manager’s Email > select Next.\n\n⚠️Note: Key Account Manager's Email should be a valid Shopee email (ends with @shopee.com). If no Key Account Manager's Email, please leave it blank.\n\n4.2.3 Third-party Partner Platform\n\n\n\n\ni) After selecting Third-party Partner Platform as your account type, you will be redirected to the Business Information section.\n\nFill in all profile details > select Next.\n\nii) Under the Services Information section, fill in your software service details and select Submit.\n\n⚠️Note: Provide your software login address and live testing account for Shopee’s verification. URL should start with “https://” and utilize a TLS 1.2 Protocol.\n\n\n\n\n4.3 Wait for your profile to be approved by Shopee\n\nOnce your application is approved, you will receive a notification email via your submitted email address.\n\n⚠️ Note: Shopee Seller applications will be processed in 3 working days, while Third-party Partner Platform applications will be processed in 10 working days.\n\n*In the ID (Indonesia) region, Shopee Seller applications will be processed within 7 working days, while Third-party Partner Platform (ISV) applications will be processed within 14 working days.\n\nIf your application isn’t approved, you can check the reason in the notification email sent to you or by selecting Go to Profile on the APP List page on Shopee Open Platform Console.\n\nSelect Edit to make the necessary changes before resubmitting.\n\n\n\nUser Guide\nDeveloper Guide\nAPI reference\nPush Mechanism\nShopee Open Platform Data Protection Policy\nShopee Markets\nService Market\nSeller Education Hub (Singapore)\nSeller Education Hub (Malaysia)\nSeller Education Hub (Thailand)\nSeller Education Hub (Vietnam)\nSeller Education Hub (Indonesia)\nSeller Education Hub (Philippines)\nSeller Education Hub (Brazil)\nSeller Education Hub (Japan)\nSeller Education Hub (Korea)\nSeller Education Hub (Hongkong)\n虾皮卖家学习中心\nSupport\nAnnouncement\nFAQ\nRaise Ticket\nCopyright @ Shopee 2025"
